Reopening this. I closed it a few weeks ago while cleaning up my forks, but the gap is still there on current main: `ChatCompletionRequest` has no `max_thinking_tokens`, so the budget gets dropped without any error.

Rebased onto bb1c98b, no conflicts. Re-checked on v0.5.20 with Qwen3.8-Flash-Next and `--enable-strict-thinking`: a budget of 64 comes back as 65 reasoning tokens, and 16384 just finishes on its own. The two tests in `test_serving_chat.py` still pass.

@JustinTong0323 could you take a look when you get a chance? It's a one-field change plus the pass-through.

